#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:7
msgid "Virtual Environments"
msgstr "虛擬環境"

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:9
msgid ""
"Python virtual environments let you isolate a project's dependencies from "
"the system Python, and xonsh works with the usual tools for creating them. "
"Whichever tool you pick, the :ref:`xcontext <aliases-xcontext>` command will "
"always tell you which interpreter, ``pip``, and environment variables are in "
"effect right now — handy when something isn't resolving where you expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:17
msgid "``virtualenv``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:19
msgid ""
"`virtualenv <https://virtualenv.pypa.io/>`_ ships with a native xonsh "
"activator, so creating and entering an environment takes just two steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:22
msgid ""
"@ virtualenv myenv\n"
"@ source myenv/bin/activate.xsh\n"
"(myenv) @"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:28
msgid "To leave the environment, run ``deactivate``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:32
msgid "``vox``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:34
msgid ""
"xonsh works with the usual Python virtual environment tools — ``venv``, "
"``virtualenv``, ``pew`` — and on top of that ships its own environments "
"manager called **Vox**. Vox is an xontrib that makes creating, listing, "
"activating, and removing virtualenvs feel natural right inside the shell, so "
"you don't have to leave the REPL or remember a separate activation script "
"per project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:41
msgid "Install and load Vox:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:43
msgid ""
"@ xpip install xontrib-vox\n"
"@ xontrib load vox"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:48
msgid "To create a new environment with vox, run ``vox new <envname>``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:51
msgid ""
"@ vox new myenv\n"
"Creating environment...\n"
"Environment \"myenv\" created. Activate it with \"vox activate myenv\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:57
msgid ""
"The interpreter ``vox`` uses to create a virtualenv is configured via the "
"``$VOX_DEFAULT_INTERPRETER`` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:59
msgid ""
"You may also set the interpreter used to create the virtual environment by "
"passing it explicitly to ``vox new`` i.e.:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:61
msgid "@ vox new python2-env -p /usr/local/bin/python2"
msgstr "@ vox new python2-env -p /usr/local/bin/python2"

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:65
msgid ""
"Under the hood, vox uses Python 3's ``venv`` module to create Python 3 "
"virtualenvs. [this is the default]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:67
msgid ""
"If a Python 2 interpreter is chosen, it will use the Python 2 interpreter's "
"``virtualenv`` module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:69
msgid ""
"By default, environments are stored in ``~/.virtualenvs``, but you can "
"override it by setting the ``$VIRTUALENV_HOME`` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:71
msgid "To see all existing environments, run ``vox list``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:73
msgid ""
"@ vox list\n"
"Available environments:\n"
"    eggs\n"
"    myenv\n"
"    spam"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:81
msgid "To activate an environment, run ``vox activate <envname>``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:83
msgid ""
"@ vox activate myenv\n"
"Activated \"myenv\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:88
msgid "Instead of ``activate``, you can call ``workon`` or ``enter``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:90
msgid ""
"If you want to activate an environment which is stored somewhere else (maybe "
"because it was created by another tool) you can pass to ``vox activate`` a "
"path to a virtual environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:93
msgid ""
"@ vox activate /home/user/myenv\n"
"Activated \"/home/user/myenv\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:98
msgid ""
"To exit the currently active environment, run ``vox deactivate`` or ``vox "
"exit``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:100
msgid ""
"@ vox deactivate\n"
"Deactivated \"myenv\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:105
msgid "To remove an environment, run ``vox remove <envname>``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:107
msgid ""
"@ vox remove myenv\n"
"Environment \"myenv\" removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:112
msgid "Instead of ``remove``, you can call ``rm``, ``delete``, or ``del``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:114
msgid ""
"To see all available commands, run ``vox help``, ``vox --help``, or ``vox -"
"h``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:117
msgid "``virtualenv`` like prompt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:118
msgid ""
"Although it's included in the default prompt, you can customize your prompt "
"to automatically update in the same way as ``virtualenv``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:121
msgid "Simply add the ``'{env_name}'`` variable to your ``$PROMPT``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:123
msgid "@ $PROMPT = '{env_name: {}}' + restofmyprompt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:127
msgid ""
"Note that you do **not** need to load the ``vox`` xontrib for this to work. "
"For more details see :ref:`customprompt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:132
msgid "Automatically Switching Environments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:134
msgid ""
"Automatic environment switching based on the current directory is managed "
"with the ``autovox`` xontrib (``xontrib load autovox``). Third-party "
"xontribs may register various policies for use with autovox. Pick and choose "
"xontribs that implement policies that match your work style."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:136
msgid ""
"Implementing policies is easy! Just register with the ``autovox_policy`` "
"event and return a ``Path`` if there is a matching venv. For example, this "
"policy implements handling if there is a ``.venv`` directory in the project:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:138
msgid ""
"@events.autovox_policy\n"
"def dotvenv_policy(path, **_):\n"
"    venv = path / '.venv'\n"
"    if venv.exists():\n"
"        return venv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:146
msgid ""
"Note that you should only return if there is an environment for this "
"directory exactly. Scanning parent directories is managed by autovox. You "
"should also make the policy check relatively cheap. (Local IO is ok, but "
"probably shouldn't call out to network services.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:150
msgid "See also"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:152
msgid ""
":ref:`aliases-xcontext` — inspect the interpreter, ``pip``, and active "
"environment variables of the current session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../python_virtual_environments.rst:154
msgid ""
":ref:`customprompt_ref` — customize ``{env_name}``, ``{env_prefix}``, and "
"``{env_postfix}`` to control how the active environment appears in the "
"prompt."
msgstr ""
